    "note": "Teaches Ch. 36 Hit 4 (Bethesda unit), Hit 5 (severity), Hit 6 (inhibitors; SIPPET), Hit 9 (emicizumab interference) and Trap 4. Checked against Müller 2022, Rühl 2026, Alvarez-Payares 2026 and Peyvandi 2026. Hit 5 mild range corrected to > 5–40 IU/dL (register flag rv-hemo-mild). Not taught: prevalence, bleeds/month, intron 22 %, inhibitor percentages, 0.5 BU sensitivity limit (source read: 0.42 BU/mL), low/high-titre cut-offs."
  },
